  "title": "Human subthalamic nucleus LFP and prefrontal subdural recordings during a working-memory encoding decision task - derivative",
  "description": "Derivative iEEG dataset of intraoperative recordings from 18 Parkinson's disease patients undergoing subthalamic nucleus deep brain stimulation surgery. It contains macroelectrode LFP from STN trajectories and subdural prefrontal strip recordings acquired during a working-memory encoding task in which participants remembered only digits shown inside a target shape. Signals are band-passed, notch-filtered, downsampled to 1 kHz and re-referenced as in the original release, and converted to BIDS with events.",
  "methods_description": "Intraoperative macroelectrode LFP from three STN trajectories and 6- and 8-contact subdural prefrontal strips were recorded during a sequential digit working-memory task. Data were band-pass filtered 1-500 Hz, notch filtered at 60 Hz, downsampled to 1 kHz, and re-referenced (macro: common average; subdural: bipolar). Int16 channel files were converted to BrainVision format with behavioural events written to events.tsv.",
